  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In neutral or faintly alkaline solution the oxidation of iodide to iodate taken place with potassium permanganate.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi>MnO</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>→</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>MnO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>OH</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>IO</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup></math>In the above reaction <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>MnO</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup></math> is an oxidising agent and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math> is a reducing agent. </p><p>Hence option D is the answer.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
